import { ensureDeepDive } from '../../scripts/task-tracker/lib/deep-dive.mjs';
import { loadConfig } from '../../scripts/task-tracker/config.mjs';

const cfg = await loadConfig();

const prose = [
  '### Where the refusal actually originates',
  '',
  '`lib/delivery-verification.mjs:517` — `if (observedMergeMethod !== intent.mergeMethod) throw',
  "verificationError('merge-method')`. The observed method is classified from the merge commit's",
  'topology (`classifyMergeMethod`); the intent method comes from configuration by way of',
  '`buildExternalIntentInput` in `verbs/deliver.mjs:283`, which sets `mergeMethod:',
  'preflight.mergeMethod`, itself resolved from `fullAutoMerge.mergeMethod` in',
  '`lib/delivery-preflight.mjs:162`. Configuration is therefore the only possible intent, and a',
  'human who merged by another method can never satisfy the equality.',
  '',
  '`verbs/close.mjs:1753` — `refuseDeliveryGate` catches the receipt error and refuses',
  'unconditionally. It never consults `--force`; the force-honoring path',
  '(`decideGateEvalFailure`) governs the close-gate checklist, a different gate. The two other',
  'candidate escapes are also closed: the no-commit lane requires zero pull requests',
  '(`lib/close-delivery-receipt.mjs:61`), and the Incorporated lane is hard-scoped to convergence',
  "issue #1381 (`verbs/incident-ledger.mjs:28`, `if (issueToken !== '1381') usageError()`).",
  '',
  '### The shape of the fix — restate the intent, never weaken the check',
  '',
  'The verifier is correct and stays byte-for-byte as it is. What is wrong is that the intent can',
  'only ever be sourced from configuration. The lane lets an operator restate the intent to match',
  'reality, explicitly and with a recorded reason, and then the unchanged equality check verifies',
  'that restatement against the observed topology.',
  '',
  'Crucially the operator cannot reconcile to a lie: the declared method is checked against the',
  'observed method before anything is written. Declaring `squash` for a two-parent merge commit',
  'refuses exactly as it does today. The lane widens who may state the intent, not what counts as',
  'proof.',
  '',
  '### Why a separate record type rather than a schema bump',
  '',
  '`lib/delivery-records.mjs` pins `aitm.delivery-intent/v1` and `aitm.delivery-receipt/v1` with',
  'strict `hasExactKeys` validation over frozen key lists (INTENT_KEYS line 29, RECEIPT_KEYS line',
  '53). Adding a divergence field to either means a v2 schema plus migration across every parser,',
  'projection, and consumer — invasive, and it churns records that are already correct.',
  '',
  'Instead the divergence is its own append-only record, `aitm.delivery-method-reconciliation/v1`,',
  'carrying configured method, observed method, operator reason, pull-request number, merge commit',
  'SHA, and accepted SHA. `lib/delivery-incident-records.mjs` is the precedent for projecting',
  'several record types together. Existing schemas are untouched; the receipt records the observed',
  'method because the intent was legitimately restated to it.',
  '',
  '### Acceptance-criterion wording to adjust at Plan',
  '',
  'AC2 as filed reads "the receipt written by that lane records the merge method actually observed',
  'and flags it as divergent from the configured intent". Under the separate-record design the',
  'receipt records the observed method, and the divergence flag lives in the reconciliation record',
  'beside it rather than inside the receipt payload. The intent of the criterion — the divergence',
  'is recorded and auditable, never silently normalized — is fully met. The wording is narrowed to',
  'name where the flag lives. This is recorded here rather than quietly edited.',
  '',
  '### Work breakdown',
  '',
  'New `lib/delivery-method-reconciliation.mjs` holding the record schema, its builder, and its',
  'validator. A `--reconcile-merge-method <method> --reason <text>` argument pair on',
  '`verbs/deliver.mjs`, valid only on the already-merged external recovery path, refusing when the',
  'pull request is unmerged, when the head does not match the accepted SHA, when the reason is',
  'empty, and when the declared method does not match observation. The reconciled method then',
  'flows into `buildExternalIntentInput` in place of the configured one. Finally',
  "`verbs/close.mjs`'s refusal message names the lane, so `--force` stops being the only",
  'discoverable escape.',
  '',
  '### Verification',
  '',
  'Unit tests for the record builder and validator, for the declared-versus-observed refusal, and',
  'for the empty-reason and unmerged-pull-request refusals. A regression test asserting',
  '`delivery-verification.mjs` still refuses a receipt naming an unobserved method — the existing',
  'behavior must be provably intact. Integration coverage for the CLI argument surface and the',
  'reworded close refusal.',
].join('\n');

const res = await ensureDeepDive({
  issueNumber: 1562,
  repo: cfg.repo,
  prose,
  posted: true,
  complete: true,
});
console.log('deep-dive:', JSON.stringify(res?.status ?? res));
